# TWO RULES:
#
#   RULE 1 (FULL UUID, unambiguous) — a canonical 8-4-4-4-12 hyphenated hex
#     UUID appearing ANYWHERE on an added '## ' line. False-positive-proof
#     against the short-SHA class BY CONSTRUCTION: a bare short SHA has no
#     internal hyphens and can never match this exact grouped shape.
#
#   RULE 2 (BARE HEX FRAGMENT, ambiguous by nature) — the FIRST whitespace-
#     delimited token immediately after '## ' is 6-8 hex characters and
#     NOTHING ELSE — the confirmed 'ad265f86' shape (first segment of a full
#     UUID, not a full UUID itself). A legitimate 'c<NNN>' counter is
#     excluded FIRST: note its own characters CAN be all hex-representable
#     ('c' is itself a valid hex nibble, so e.g. a hypothetical 5-digit
#     'c12345' counter would otherwise collide) — the '^c[0-9]+$' shape check
#     must run before the hex-fragment check, not alongside it. Ambiguous
#     residual risk this rule accepts and documents rather than pretends to
#     close: a future fixed SOURCE LABEL that happens to be an all-hex-letter
#     word (e.g. 'facade', 'decade') would still collide — WARN-only by
#     design (never escalated to reject, regardless of
#     GIT_NOTEBOOK_UUID_PROVENANCE_MODE), with a documented escape hatch.
#
# ESCAPE HATCH (mirrors task-claim-owner-session-lint.sh's own convention):
# a 'notebook-uuid-lint-allow: <reason>' comment anywhere on the same heading
# line suppresses BOTH rules for that one line.
#
